etm-powersync-plugins-modbus (1.15.2+etm6) trixie; urgency=medium

  * sunspec: package the vendored SunSpec plugin as nymea-plugin-sunspec-etm01.
    The plugin was added to the build by the vendoring commit but never
    packaged, so dh_missing found its .so in debian/tmp with nowhere to install
    it and aborted the whole source package: no binary package at all came out
    of this branch, not even for the four unrelated plugins.
  * sunspec: add the Fronius vendor. A GEN24 answers for the inverter on one
    unit ID and for its Smart Meter on another, behind the same host and port,
    so one froniusConnection thing now carries two SunSpecConnection objects.
    The meter connection is brought up only once the primary has finished
    discovering, and the parent connected state follows the primary alone.
  * sunspec: correct the storage setpoint chain - charge and discharge rates
    read back from InWRte/OutWRte instead of the read-only gradients, the rate
    range widened to -100..100 so forced charging can be expressed at all,
    enableDischarging reconciled from StorCtl_Mod, and the revert timer armed
    with every setpoint so one left behind by a stopped HEMS expires.
  * debian: add libnymea-sunspec-dev to Build-Depends. Upstream does not need
    it because it builds libnymea-sunspec from the same source tree; this
    repository vendors only the plugin and links against the installed library.
  * The new binary package conflicts with, replaces and provides
    nymea-plugin-sunspec: it ships the same plugin file and the same pluginId
    as the upstream package this repository already mirrors.

